Z||000000||MachineHead||12-07-2000||08:31 AM||||I'm kinda new to Fieros and have no clue as what you guys are talking about sometimes.  Could you help me out?<BR>Whats:<BR>2m4, 2m6, 2m8?<BR>Duke?<BR>I know there was more, but I can't think of it now.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||12-07-2000||08:41 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MachineHead:<BR><B>I'm kinda new to Fieros and have no clue as what you guys are talking about sometimes.  Could you help me out?<BR>Whats:<BR>2m4, 2m6, 2m8?<BR>Duke?<BR>I know there was more, but I can't think of it now.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hi MachineHead,<P>The 2M means 2= Two Seater M= Mid-Engine. The last number is the engine size. 4cyl-6cyl<P>There is no 2M8. Thats just people call the coupes that some put V8's in.<P>The Duke is the name of the 4cyl engine (Iron Duke) <P><BR>What else would you like to know?? Thats why were here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">     <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 12-07-2000).]||||reg||10
